      "text": {
        "title": "Guten Morgen auf Station",
        "de": "Guten Morgen. Ich bin Dr. Weber. Sie sind Herr Yilmaz. Das ist die Spritze. Sie liegt hier. Das ist das Thermometer. Es liegt hier. Wir arbeiten auf Station 3B.",
        "en": "Good morning. I am Dr Weber. You are Mr Yilmaz. This is the syringe. It is here. This is the thermometer. It is here. We work on ward 3B."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dialogue",
      "type": "dialogue",
      "label": "Dialogue",
      "title": "Who is who on ward 3B",
      "instructions": "Tap any German word. Notice capital Sie for the patient.",
      "scene": "Station 3B, 7:00. Dr. Weber meets Herr Yilmaz. Anna, the nurse, is there too.",
      "sceneTitle": "Aufnahme auf Station 3B",
      "speakers": {
        "A": {
          "name": "Dr. Weber",
          "role": "Ärztin",
          "avatar": "👩‍⚕️"
        },
        "P": {
          "name": "Herr Yilmaz",
          "role": "Patient",
          "avatar": "🧑🏽"
        },
        "N": {
          "name": "Anna",
          "role": "Pflegekraft",
          "avatar": "🧑‍⚕️"
        }
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "who": "A",
          "de": "Guten Morgen. Ich bin Dr. Weber. Wer sind Sie?",
          "en": "Good morning. I am Dr Weber. Who are you?"
        },
        {
          "who": "P",
          "de": "Ich bin Herr Yilmaz.",
          "en": "I am Mr Yilmaz."
        },
        {
          "who": "N",
          "de": "Ich bin Anna. Ich bin die Pflegekraft. Wir sind auf Station 3B.",
          "en": "I am Anna. I am the nurse. We are on ward 3B."
        },
        {
          "who": "A",
          "de": "Das ist die Spritze. Sie liegt hier. Das Thermometer? Es liegt auch hier.",
          "en": "This is the syringe. It is here. The thermometer? It is here too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "Pronouns for people and things",
      "heroTitle": "One pronoun, four jobs for sie",
      "story": [
        "On the ward you need nine pronouns. <b>ich</b> is you speaking. <b>du</b> is one person you know. <b>Sie</b> — always capital — is a patient or a colleague you do not know well.",
        "Things follow the article. <b>der</b> Arzt → <b>er</b>. <b>die</b> Spritze → <b>sie</b>. <b>das</b> Thermometer → <b>es</b>. Plural things also take <b>sie</b>."
      ],
      "tables": [
